<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Lower Yafa Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1967 CE (approx.) · capital Al Qara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The sultanate of the Afifi family over the lower Yafa highlands north-east of Aden, a small British-protected state until 1967.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a> tribes of the mountains north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> threw off the authority of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qasimid-state">Qasimid State</a> in the early 18th century. The confederation split into an upper and a lower part, and the Afifi family established the Lower Yafa sultanate, with its seat at Al Qara.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultan was more an arbiter among tribes than a ruler with an administration. The region's terraced highlands produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and grain, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a>'i men were known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, serving the sultans of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hadramawt">Hadramawt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a>. Lower Yafa signed a protection treaty with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Aden Protectorate</a>, joining the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south">Federation of Arab Emirates of the South</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>It was a member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a> until 1967, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took over and the territory was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lower-yafa-sultanate.jpg" alt="Lower Yafa Sultanate" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lower_Yafa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Al Qara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lower Yafa, Sultanate of Lower Yafa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=lower-yafa-sultanate" aria-label="Lower Yafa Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5922 1685 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lower Yafa Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6242 1941L6295 1853M6242 1941L6313 1863M6242 1941L6313 1863M6242 1941L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6295 1853h0M6313 1863h0M6313 1863h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6242 1941h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6242 1941h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=lower-yafa-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
